pis"},{"text":"அம்","lemma":"அம்","gloss":"adjectival suffix"}],"gloss":"of calotropis"},{"surface":"கண்ணியும்","parts":[{"text":"கண்ணி","lemma":"கண்ணி","gloss":"garland"},{"text":"உம்","lemma":"உம்","gloss":"even"}],"gloss":"even the garland"},{"surface":"சூடுப","parts":[{"text":"சூடு","lemma":"சூடு","gloss":"wear"},{"text":"ப","lemma":"ப","gloss":"they (suffix)"}],"gloss":"they will wear"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"மறுகின்","parts":[{"text":"மறுகு","lemma":"மறுகு","gloss":"street"},{"text":"இன்","lemma":"இன்","gloss":"locative suffix"}],"gloss":"in the street"},{"surface":"ஆர்க்கவும்","parts":[{"text":"ஆர்க்கவும்","lemma":"ஆர்க்கவும்","gloss":"to be shouted at also"}],"gloss":"to be shouted at also","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"படுப","parts":[{"text":"படு","lemma":"படு","gloss":"undergo"},{"text":"ப","lemma":"ப","gloss":"they (suffix)"}],"gloss":"they will undergo"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"பிறிதும்","parts":[{"text":"பிறிது","lemma":"பிறிது","gloss":"other thing"},{"text":"உம்","lemma":"உம்","gloss":"even"}],"gloss":"other things also"},{"surface":"ஆகுப","parts":[{"text":"ஆகு","lemma":"ஆகு","gloss":"happen"},{"text":"ப","lemma":"ப","gloss":"they (suffix)"}],"gloss":"they will do"},{"surface":"காமம்","parts":[{"text":"காமம்","lemma":"காமம்","gloss":"love"}],"gloss":"love"},{"surface":"காழ்","parts":[{"text":"காழ்","lemma":"காழ்","gloss":"core"}],"gloss":"sturdiness"},{"surface":"கொளினே","parts":[{"text":"கொள்","lemma":"கொள்","gloss":"take"},{"text":"இன்","lemma":"இன்","gloss":"if"},{"text":"ஏ","lemma":"ஏ","gloss":"emphasis"}],"gloss":"if it takes"}]}],"literal":"As a horse, even a palmyra stem they will ride; as a flower, / even a garland of closed buds of calotropis they will wear; / in the street, to be shouted at they will undergo; / other things also they will do, if love takes deep root.","translation":"They will ride a palmyra stem as if it were a horse. They will wear a garland of closed calotropis buds as if they were flowers. They will suffer being shouted at in the public streets. They will do even other things, if love takes deep root.","modern":"காதல் உறுதியானால், பனை மடலைக் குதிரை என்று ஏறி நடத்துவார்கள்; குவிந்த எருக்கம் மொட்டுகளாலான மாலையைப் பூமாலை என்று சூடிக் கொள்வார்கள்; தெருவில் எல்லாரும் ஆரவாரம் செய்யும்படித் துன்பப்படுவார்கள்; வேறு பலவற்றையும் செய்வார்கள்.","explanation":"This poem is spoken by the hero to himself or to his friend, expressing the desperate intensity of his love. He declares that when love takes deep root and matures, a lover loses all sense of shame and social propriety. He is willing to ride the 'maṭal mā' (a mock horse made of sharp palmyra stems) to proclaim his love publicly, wearing a garland of useless, bitter calotropis (erukku) flowers. He is ready to endure the mockery and shouting of the townspeople in the streets. The imagery of the palmyra horse and calotropis garland highlights the uncontrollable, desperate nature of his desire.","model":"gemini-3.5-flash"}}